  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Toluene reacts with chlorine in the presence of light to give Benzal chloride. The reaction happens between methylbenzene and chlorine in the presence of ultraviolet light - typically sunlight. This is a good example of a photochemical reaction - a reaction brought about by light.</p><p>Benzyl chloride on reaction with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>373</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> gives benzaldehyde.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cf7df457-312f-4d4f-b6ea-fda7974a8343.png\" style=\"width: 900px; height: 246px;\"/></p>",
